  },
  {
   "id": "a_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 578,
   "y": 168,
   "width": 464,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100008,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700056,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "interface EventApplier\n  apply(state: MutableState, event) -> void\n\nMutableState. A PURE function: no clock, no I/O,\nno randomness. Runs on EVERY replay.",
   "originalText": "interface EventApplier\n  apply(state: MutableState, event) -> void\n\nMutableState. A PURE function: no clock, no I/O,\nno randomness. Runs on EVERY replay.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "a",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 286,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100009,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700063,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Different state TYPES, deliberately: apply() has no handle on which to call an external service, and no legitimate reason to\nreach for now(). The compiler helps. Projection.rebuild() is likewise on the interface as a first-class operation rather than\nan admin script - it is what makes a projection bug retroactively fixable, so every author must think about whether theirs\ncan actually be rebuilt.",
   "originalText": "Different state TYPES, deliberately: apply() has no handle on which to call an external service, and no legitimate reason to\nreach for now(). The compiler helps. Projection.rebuild() is likewise on the interface as a first-class operation rather than\nan admin script - it is what makes a projection bug retroactively fixable, so every author must think about whether theirs\ncan actually be rebuilt.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d2",
